      "message": "The new sequence looks right to me, and the message now explains why the reserved ASID is enough.\n\nThe subject is 73 columns, though, and three body lines are 73-74 (the ones ending in \"page table.\", \"entry points.\" and \"against TCR,\"). Would something like this work for the subject?\n\n```\nANDROID: P3S: arm64/mm: Isolate old translations before geometry change\n```\n\nCould the body also start with what goes wrong without the patch? As far as I can see, since aosp/4312469 the geometry changes while TTBR0 and the ASID still belong to the previous mm. For example:\n\n```\nSince \"ANDROID: P3S: arm64: mm: Switch TCR_EL1.TG0 and T0SZ on context\nswitch\", check_and_switch_context() changes TCR_EL1.TG0/T0SZ while\nTTBR0 and the ASID in TTBR1 still belong to the previous mm, unless CnP\nor emulated PAN has installed the reserved TTBR0. A speculative walk can\nthen decode the previous mm\u0027s tables with the new granule and cache the\nresult under that mm\u0027s ASID.\n```",
